WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.314 --> 00:00:18.807
"I'm hungry," Bajie moaned.

2
00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:22.230
stomach grumbled loudly.

3
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.313
"Can we stop walking?"

4
00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:28.976
"We'll stop for lunch soon," said the Tang Monk.

5
00:00:29.884 --> 00:00:31.925
weather is nice, and the road is smooth.

6
00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:33.765
I want to keep moving.

7
00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:36.246
I'm eager to reach the Western Paradise."

8
00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:42.568
laughed. "Master, I don't know why you're still going there.

9
00:00:43.548 --> 00:00:46.009
You should have married that scorpion spirit instead!"

10
00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:48.390
Tang Monk frowned.

11
00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.350
"That's not funny, Wukong."

12
00:00:51.711 --> 00:00:53.911
agree with Wukong," said Bajie.

13
00:00:53.931 --> 00:00:57.536
"I would have gladly married her."

14
00:00:58.097 --> 00:00:59.158
raised an eyebrow.

15
00:00:59.178 --> 00:01:01.259
"I doubt she would have married you."

16
00:01:02.881 --> 00:01:05.463
not?" Bajie puffed out his chest.

17
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:07.785
"I'm very handsome!"

18
00:01:08.966 --> 00:01:11.548
Everybody laughed, including Bajie.

19
00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.033
They had continued for another hour when the pig complained again.

20
00:01:18.053 --> 00:01:21.996
"My legs are tired," he said.

21
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:26.100
"We'll stop at the next village," said the Tang Monk.

22
00:01:27.905 --> 00:01:28.885
Bajie sighed.

23
00:01:28.905 --> 00:01:31.987
"I hope we reach the next village soon."

24
00:01:32.007 --> 00:01:36.851
"I know how we can get there soon," said Wukong with a laugh.

25
00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:41.514
The monkey smacked the horse, which shot forward.

26
00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:45.737
"Wukong!" cried the Tang Monk, hanging on tightly.

27
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.883
When the horse finally stopped running, the monk was far ahead of his companions.

28
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.322
A group of nasty-looking men stood in front of him.

29
00:02:00.342 --> 00:02:02.984
"Give us all your money!"

30
00:02:03.385 --> 00:02:04.606
said a man with an ax.

31
00:02:05.927 --> 00:02:07.608
The Tang Monk shook with fear.

32
00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:10.430
Wukong was already running over.

33
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.152
"Don't you dare harm my master!"

34
00:02:13.492 --> 00:02:14.313
shouted the monkey.

35
00:02:18.516 --> 00:02:19.197
are you?"

36
00:02:19.577 --> 00:02:20.258
asked the man.

37
00:02:20.278 --> 00:02:23.140
"My name is Sun Wukong."

38
00:02:26.372 --> 00:02:29.853
"Give me your money, Sun Wukong," said the man.

39
00:02:32.194 --> 00:02:34.155
don't have much money," said the monkey.

40
00:02:34.175 --> 00:02:36.216
"You'd better give me yours."

41
00:02:38.297 --> 00:02:39.857
man's face turned red.

42
00:02:39.877 --> 00:02:42.318
"I'm not going to give you money!"

43
00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:45.840
"Let's make a bet then," said Wukong.

44
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.262
He pulled out his iron bar, which quickly grew to the height of a person.

45
00:02:51.422 --> 00:02:52.563
The men looked nervous.

46
00:02:53.703 --> 00:02:55.724
The monkey stood the bar on the ground.

47
00:02:57.128 --> 00:03:00.291
"If you can pick this up, we'll give you all of our money."

48
00:03:01.872 --> 00:03:04.214
a fool," said the man with an ax.

49
00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:08.458
"I'm sure I can pick that bar up."

50
00:03:08.598 --> 00:03:10.940
"Go ahead and try," said Wukong.

51
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.262
The man put down the ax.

52
00:03:14.563 --> 00:03:18.106
He grasped the bar with his hands and tried to lift it.

53
00:03:18.126 --> 00:03:22.929
"It's heavier than it looks," said the man.

54
00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.331
tried to lift the bar again.

55
00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.453
Sweat poured down his red face.

56
00:03:28.873 --> 00:03:30.434
But the bar didn't budge.

57
00:03:30.454 --> 00:03:33.256
"Now it's my turn!"

58
00:03:33.496 --> 00:03:34.256
said Wukong.

59
00:03:35.437 --> 00:03:38.659
He lifted the bar over his head and twirled it around.

60
00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.300
eyes flashed with anger.

61
00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.421
He got ready to strike the man.

62
00:03:43.481 --> 00:03:46.143
"Wukong, don't!"

63
00:03:46.423 --> 00:03:47.424
shouted the Tang Monk.

64
00:03:49.825 --> 00:03:51.166
The man took a step back.

65
00:03:52.486 --> 00:03:54.968
Suddenly the bar dropped from Wukong's hands.

66
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.801
"Aargh!" cried the monkey, holding his head.

67
00:03:59.902 --> 00:04:04.625
He fell to his knees as the Tang Monk quietly recited the Tight Headband spell.

68
00:04:05.626 --> 00:04:08.548
The robbers glanced at one another and then ran away.

69
00:04:09.729 --> 00:04:13.491
When the monk stopped reciting the spell, Wukong was furious.

70
00:04:14.692 --> 00:04:15.793
did you do that?"

71
00:04:16.013 --> 00:04:16.553
he cried.

72
00:04:16.573 --> 00:04:20.996
"They were going "You must not hurt people!"

73
00:04:21.237 --> 00:04:22.097
commanded the monk.

74
00:04:22.117 --> 00:04:26.100
"I destroy demons all the time," said the monkey.

75
00:04:28.616 --> 00:04:29.858
fine to hurt demons.

76
00:04:30.558 --> 00:04:34.522
But you must not hurt monk sighed.

77
00:04:34.542 --> 00:04:37.264
"You're still evil, Wukong.

78
00:04:38.445 --> 00:04:40.286
can't bring you to the Western Paradise.

79
00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.408
You must leave."

80
00:04:46.512 --> 00:04:48.033
you need me, Master!"

81
00:04:48.313 --> 00:04:49.454
Wukong insisted.

82
00:04:49.474 --> 00:04:52.017
"I refuse to leave."

83
00:04:54.118 --> 00:04:55.780
"Go!" said the Tang Monk.

84
00:04:56.712 --> 00:05:00.274
"Or I'll recite the Tight Headband spell until your head explodes!"

85
00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.777
Wukong could see that the monk wasn't going to change his mind.

86
00:05:06.977 --> 00:05:11.660
With tears in his eyes, the monkey leaped into the air and was gone.
